      "id": "a0",
      "pos": 1,
      "text": "The Vinland Map is a world map that depicts a landmass labelled \"Vinlanda Insula\" to the west of Greenland.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "pos": 2,
      "text": "The map surfaced in 1957 bound together with a manuscript copy of the Tartar Relation.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "pos": 3,
      "text": "Matching wormholes connected the map, the Tartar Relation, and a copy of Vincent of Beauvais's Speculum Historiale.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "pos": 4,
      "text": "Yale University published the map in 1965 in the volume \"The Vinland Map and the Tartar Relation\".",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "pos": 5,
      "text": "The map was donated to the British Library in 1965.",
      "factual": false,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "pos": 6,
      "text": "Radiocarbon dating carried out in 2002 placed the map's parchment at about the year 1434.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "pos": 7,
      "text": "Anatase pigment of the kind found in the ink was first manufactured commercially in the 1920s.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "pos": 8,
      "text": "Walter McCrone's 1974 microscopic analysis of the ink detected anatase, a form of titanium dioxide.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "pos": 9,
      "text": "Thomas Cahill's 1987 proton-induced X-ray emission study found only trace amounts of titanium in the map's ink.",
      "factual": true,
      "stance": "asserted"
    },
    {
